# ========== GOOGLE CLOUD CREDENTIALS ==========

# Required: path to your Google Cloud service-account JSON key.
# This file is a credential -- never commit it or share it.
# If this is unset, Starling falls back to Google's own standard variable,
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS. See the README section
# "Set Up Google Cloud Credentials" for how to create a key.
STARLING_GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS=~/starling-service-account.json

# ========== DIRECTORIES ==========

# Optional: the root Starling works under. Every directory and log below defaults
# to a subdirectory of this one, so setting this alone relocates everything.
# Default: ~/Starling
# STARLING_HOME=~/Starling

# Optional: where Starling looks for .txt files to read aloud.
# Default: <STARLING_HOME>/input
# STARLING_INPUT_DIR=

# Optional: where the generated .wav files are written.
# Default: <STARLING_HOME>/output
# STARLING_OUTPUT_DIR=

# Optional: where input files are moved after they are read successfully.
# Default: <STARLING_HOME>/archive
# STARLING_ARCHIVE_DIR=

# ========== LOGS ==========

# Optional: the character-usage log. Starling appends one line per file with a
# running monthly total, so you can see what you are billing yourself for.
# Default: <STARLING_HOME>/logs/usage.log
# STARLING_USAGE_LOG=

# Optional: the error log.
# Default: <STARLING_HOME>/logs/errors.log
# STARLING_ERROR_LOG=

# ========== VOICE ==========

# Optional: BCP-47 language tag Starling synthesizes in. Default: en-US
# STARLING_LANGUAGE_CODE=en-US

# Optional: how Starling picks a voice.
#   random -- pick a different voice from STARLING_VOICE_POOL for each file (default)
#   fixed  -- always use STARLING_VOICE_NAME
# STARLING_VOICE_MODE=random

# Optional: the voice used when STARLING_VOICE_MODE=fixed.
# Default: en-US-Chirp3-HD-Enceladus
# Run `starling voices` to list every voice Google offers for your language.
# BILLING: voice families are priced differently -- Chirp 3: HD, Neural2, Studio
# and Standard are not the same rate, and you are billed on your own Google Cloud
# account. Check https://cloud.google.com/text-to-speech/pricing before switching
# families.
# STARLING_VOICE_NAME=en-US-Chirp3-HD-Enceladus

# Optional: comma-separated voice names to draw from when STARLING_VOICE_MODE=random.
# Unset uses Starling's default pool: the 22 Chirp 3: HD en-US voices. Whitespace
# around names is ignored and duplicates are dropped. Setting this to a list with no
# names in it is an error, not a silent fallback -- unset the variable instead. The
# BILLING note above applies to every family you put in the pool.
# STARLING_VOICE_POOL=en-US-Chirp3-HD-Aoede,en-US-Chirp3-HD-Puck,en-US-Chirp3-HD-Charon

# ========== MIGRATION ==========
# Starling 0.1 renamed the old TTS_* variables. TTS_VOICE_NAME is now
# STARLING_VOICE_NAME, TTS_LANGUAGE_CODE is now STARLING_LANGUAGE_CODE, and
# TTS_MODEL was removed (it was read but never used). The old names are ignored.
